WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.462
What does UV light do to your

00:00:01.508 --> 00:00:02.066
DNA?

00:00:02.693 --> 00:00:04.364
Watch these two neighbors, a C and

00:00:04.399 --> 00:00:04.864
a T.

00:00:05.583 --> 00:00:06.710
UV light hits them.

00:00:07.162 --> 00:00:08.869
Now they're stuck together by a covalent

00:00:08.916 --> 00:00:10.785
bond, a strong chemical link.

00:00:11.412 --> 00:00:13.130
That bond bends the backbone into a

00:00:13.176 --> 00:00:13.618
bulge.

00:00:14.152 --> 00:00:15.591
Like a kink in a garden hose.

00:00:16.125 --> 00:00:18.052
The bulge stops genes from being copied

00:00:18.099 --> 00:00:18.621
normally.

00:00:19.469 --> 00:00:21.477
UV light bonds neighboring C's and T's

00:00:21.524 --> 00:00:23.045
together, which makes a bulge.

00:00:23.672 --> 00:00:24.496
How is it fixed?

00:00:25.216 --> 00:00:25.831
Swipe.
